["<aside class=\"callout why\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Why it matters</div><p>Most beginners walk through the bush at a hiking pace. Deer hear and see them long before. Slow down and the woods change.</p></aside><figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Bar chart: time to cover 200 metres of timber. Hiking pace, about 3 minutes, a short bar. Still hunting, 30 minutes or more, a long bar. Most beginners walk at hiking pace.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Time to cover 200 m of timber</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">Hiking pace</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"94\" width=\"24\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#c0392b\"/>\n  <text x=\"54\" y=\"121\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">about 3 min (Tip)</text>\n  <text x=\"20\" y=\"174\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">Still hunting</text>\n  <rect x=\"20\" y=\"184\" width=\"300\" height=\"40\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <text x=\"170\" y=\"210\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">30 min or more (Tip)</text>\n  <polygon points=\"320,184 344,204 320,224\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"270\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Slow down and the woods change</text>\n</svg>\n</figure>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Two panels. Still hunting: in thick timber, you creep slowly, searching for a deer you have not seen yet. Stalking: in open country, you have already seen the deer and close the distance using cover.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"8\" y=\"44\" width=\"188\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#c6d1b5\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"44\" width=\"188\" height=\"200\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Still hunting</text>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"32\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Stalking</text>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\"><polygon points=\"30,110 42,74 54,110\"/><polygon points=\"80,90 92,54 104,90\"/><polygon points=\"140,120 152,84 164,120\"/><polygon points=\"40,200 52,164 64,200\"/><polygon points=\"150,210 162,174 174,210\"/><polygon points=\"100,150 112,114 124,150\"/></g>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"220\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"70\" y=\"186\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">?</text><text x=\"126\" y=\"176\" font-size=\"26\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">?</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(330 80)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"14\" cy=\"-8\" r=\"5\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><circle cx=\"250\" cy=\"200\" r=\"14\"/><circle cx=\"280\" cy=\"150\" r=\"14\"/><circle cx=\"300\" cy=\"110\" r=\"12\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M240 228 C 236 200, 268 180, 272 160 S 290 124, 296 120\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\" stroke-dasharray=\"6 5\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"240\" cy=\"228\" r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"102\" y=\"266\">deer not seen yet</text><text x=\"102\" y=\"284\">thick timber, quiet days</text>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"266\">deer already seen</text><text x=\"298\" y=\"284\">open country, after glassing</text></g>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li><strong>Still hunting:</strong> slow walking through cover to find a deer <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Stalking:</strong> closing in on a deer you have already seen <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: still hunting vs stalking, in full</summary><ul><li><strong>Still hunting:</strong> walking very slowly through deer cover, hoping to see a deer before it sees you <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li><strong>Stalking:</strong> you have already seen the deer. You close the distance for a shot <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">70%</span>.</li><li>Still hunting suits thick timber and wet, quiet days.</li><li>Stalking suits open country after <button class=\"term\" data-term=\"Glassing\">Glassing</button>.</li><li>Both depend on wind. Read the wind session first.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4iDY9z3ldKE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Steven Rinella Explains the Difference Between Still, Ambush, and Spot and Stalk Hunting</b><small>Three ways to hunt: still, ambush, spot and stalk.<br>MeatEater, YouTube, 3 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of still hunting cadence, top view. The hunter takes 3 slow steps, then stops and scans left and right for 20 seconds or more. Then 3 more steps and another long stop. Look much more than you walk.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#2f3a2b\" opacity=\".8\"><polygon points=\"60,90 72,58 84,90\"/><polygon points=\"200,70 212,38 224,70\"/><polygon points=\"330,100 342,68 354,100\"/><polygon points=\"120,270 132,238 144,270\"/><polygon points=\"280,262 292,230 304,262\"/></g>\n  <g fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n    <ellipse cx=\"50\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.3s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n    <ellipse cx=\"95\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"0.9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n    <ellipse cx=\"140\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"1.5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n    <ellipse cx=\"185\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.0s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n    <ellipse cx=\"230\" cy=\"160\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"5.6s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n    <ellipse cx=\"275\" cy=\"180\" rx=\"10\" ry=\"6\" opacity=\"0\"><set attributeName=\"opacity\" to=\"1\" begin=\"6.2s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></ellipse>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"20 170;50 170;95 170;140 170;140 170;185 170;230 170;275 170;275 170\" keyTimes=\"0;0.03;0.09;0.15;0.5;0.53;0.59;0.65;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <g opacity=\"0\">\n      <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.16;0.17;0.48;0.49;0.66;0.67;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n      <path d=\"M0 0 L90 -45 A 100 100 0 0 1 90 45 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".2\">\n        <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"-50;50;-50;50;0\" dur=\"3s\" begin=\"1.7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"rotate\" values=\"0;-50;50;-50;0\" dur=\"3s\" begin=\"6.7s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n      </path>\n    </g>\n    <circle r=\"11\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;0;1;1;0;0;1;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.16;0.17;0.48;0.49;0.66;0.67;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"110\" y=\"16\" width=\"180\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">STOP. Look 20 s +</text>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"1\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;1;0;0;1;1;0;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.16;0.17;0.48;0.49;0.66;0.67;1\" dur=\"10s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"39\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2 or 3 slow steps</text>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"9s\" dur=\".5s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"60\" y=\"230\" width=\"280\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n    <text x=\"200\" y=\"253\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Look much more than you walk</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>2 or 3 steps, then a long look. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Move 2 or 3 steps, then stand and look 20 seconds or more (Tip).</li><li>A few hundred metres an hour is normal (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: pace in full</summary><ul><li>Move 2 or 3 steps, then stand and look for 20 seconds or more. Some hunters stop for minutes (Tip, hunter method).</li><li>Look much more than you walk <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Expect to cover very little ground: a few hundred metres an hour is normal (Tip).</li><li>Look near as well as far. A bedded deer may be very close <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Before each step, pick where your foot goes next.</li><li>Heel down softly, roll to the ball, test before putting weight on it <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Q_RRC3Tmkq4\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>Extra Tips For The Still Hunter With Janis Putelis</b><small>Still hunting is mostly standing still. Step, stop, look.<br>MeatEater, YouTube, 4 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<div class=\"steps\" data-n=\"4\"><div class=\"steps-head\"><b>One quiet step in 4 moves</b><span class=\"steps-count\">1 of 4</span></div><div class=\"steps-track\"><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Foot step 1: before you step, look down and pick a clear spot for the next foot. Avoid the dry stick.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"5\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"5\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(120 180) rotate(-10)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -70 L34 -70 L40 -30 L90 -22 C 104 -18, 104 0, 92 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-4\" width=\"96\" height=\"8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"5\"><line x1=\"290\" y1=\"226\" x2=\"340\" y2=\"220\"/></g><path d=\"M300 200 L330 240 M330 200 L300 240\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"4\"/><ellipse cx=\"230\" cy=\"230\" rx=\"30\" ry=\"6\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" opacity=\".6\"/><text x=\"230\" y=\"214\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">clear spot</text><text x=\"316\" y=\"190\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">dry stick</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">1. Pick the spot first</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Eyes down for a moment, then step</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>1.</b> Pick a clear spot for the next foot.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Foot step 2: set the heel down softly, toe still raised.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"5\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"5\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(170 226) rotate(-22)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -70 L34 -70 L40 -30 L90 -22 C 104 -18, 104 0, 92 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-4\" width=\"96\" height=\"8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><path d=\"M150 236 L190 236\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><text x=\"260\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">heel first,</text><text x=\"260\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">soft</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">2. Heel down softly</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Do not put weight on it yet</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>2.</b> Set the heel down softly.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Foot step 3: roll slowly from the heel to the ball of the foot, feeling for sticks.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"5\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"5\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(150 226) rotate(0)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -70 L34 -70 L40 -30 L90 -22 C 104 -18, 104 0, 92 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-4\" width=\"96\" height=\"8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><path d=\"M200 190 C 230 170, 250 180, 252 200\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><polygon points=\"246,198 258,198 252,210\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"270\" y=\"160\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">roll to the ball</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">3. Roll to the ball</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Feel for sticks through the sole</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>3.</b> Roll slowly to the ball of the foot.</figcaption></figure><figure class=\"step-frame\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Foot step 4: test before you commit. If it is quiet, put your full weight on it. If something cracks, lift the foot and move it.\"><rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"230\" width=\"400\" height=\"70\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/><g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><ellipse cx=\"60\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"20\" ry=\"5\"/><ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"232\" rx=\"24\" ry=\"5\"/></g><g transform=\"translate(150 226) rotate(0)\"><path d=\"M0 0 L0 -70 L34 -70 L40 -30 L90 -22 C 104 -18, 104 0, 92 0 Z\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/><rect x=\"-2\" y=\"-4\" width=\"96\" height=\"8\" rx=\"3\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/></g><path d=\"M196 110 L196 150\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/><polygon points=\"186,146 206,146 196,162\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><text x=\"210\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">quiet? then</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">full weight</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"120\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">crack?</text><text x=\"70\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">lift, move</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"30\" font-size=\"18\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">4. Test, then weight</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Heel, roll, test: then the next step (65%)</text></svg>\n<figcaption><b>4.</b> Quiet? Full weight. Crack? Lift and move.</figcaption></figure></div><div class=\"steps-nav\"><button class=\"steps-prev\" aria-label=\"Back\">‹ Back</button><span class=\"steps-dots\"><i></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><button class=\"steps-next\" aria-label=\"Next\">Next ›</button></div></div>","<figure class=\"diagram anim\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Animation of a stalk, top view. A deer feeds with its head down. The hunter moves from one bush to the next only while the head is down. Each time the deer lifts its head, the hunter freezes. After three moves the hunter is behind the last bush, in range, wind in the face.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#efe6cf\"/>\n  <g stroke=\"#4a7fb0\" stroke-width=\"3\" fill=\"none\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" opacity=\".8\">\n    <path d=\"M370 40 l-40 30 m4 -12 l-4 12 l12 -2\"><animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"0 0;-10 8;0 0\" dur=\"2s\" repeatCount=\"indefinite\"/></path>\n  </g>\n  <text x=\"388\" y=\"24\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\" text-anchor=\"end\">wind in your face</text>\n  <g fill=\"#8a9a6b\"><circle cx=\"90\" cy=\"236\" r=\"20\"/><circle cx=\"160\" cy=\"180\" r=\"20\"/><circle cx=\"230\" cy=\"140\" r=\"18\"/><circle cx=\"268\" cy=\"110\" r=\"16\"/></g>\n  <g>\n    <ellipse cx=\"330\" cy=\"90\" rx=\"22\" ry=\"11\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n    <circle cx=\"308\" cy=\"104\" r=\"7\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\">\n      <animate attributeName=\"cy\" values=\"104;72;104;72;104\" keyTimes=\"0;0.22;0.39;0.66;0.78\" calcMode=\"discrete\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    </circle>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <animateTransform attributeName=\"transform\" type=\"translate\" values=\"66 252;66 252;140 196;140 196;140 196;212 156;212 156;212 156;252 126;252 126\" keyTimes=\"0;0.03;0.2;0.22;0.4;0.62;0.66;0.79;0.95;1\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <circle r=\"9\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  </g>\n  <g>\n    <text x=\"12\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\">Head down: move\n      <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"1;0;1;0;1\" keyTimes=\"0;0.22;0.39;0.66;0.78\" calcMode=\"discrete\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n    <text x=\"12\" y=\"290\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" opacity=\"0\">Head up: FREEZE\n      <animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1;0;1;0\" keyTimes=\"0;0.22;0.39;0.66;0.78\" calcMode=\"discrete\" dur=\"9s\" fill=\"freeze\"/></text>\n  </g>\n  <g opacity=\"0\"><animate attributeName=\"opacity\" values=\"0;1\" begin=\"8.6s\" dur=\".4s\" fill=\"freeze\"/>\n    <rect x=\"220\" y=\"244\" width=\"170\" height=\"44\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n    <text x=\"305\" y=\"272\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">In range, hidden</text>\n  </g>\n</svg>\n<figcaption>Head down: move. Head up: freeze. <button class=\"anim-replay\">↻ Replay</button></figcaption></figure><ul><li>Move from cover to cover. Pause at each.</li><li>Stay in shade, off the skyline.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: using cover, in full</summary><ul><li>Move when the deer's head is down feeding or behind a tree (Tip).</li><li>Stay in shade. Avoid the skyline on ridges.</li><li>Keep a tree or bush between you and where deer may be, then look around it, not over it (Tip).</li><li>Move from one piece of cover to the next. Pause at each.</li><li>Freeze when a deer looks up. Wait until it relaxes (Tip).</li></ul></details><a class=\"yt-card\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_JTWhL-qTdk\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span class=\"yt-play\">▶</span><span class=\"yt-text\"><b>5 Spot and Stalk Hunting Tips!</b><small>Five spot and stalk tips for open country.<br>Informed Outdoors, YouTube, 5 min. Needs internet.</small></span></a>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Look around cover, not over it. Left, crossed: a head pokes up over the top of a bush, a round shape against the sky. Right, ticked: the hunter looks around the side of a tree trunk, low and in shade.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect x=\"0\" y=\"240\" width=\"400\" height=\"60\" fill=\"#c9b79c\"/>\n  <ellipse cx=\"100\" cy=\"200\" rx=\"70\" ry=\"46\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"148\" r=\"16\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M60 60 L140 120 M140 60 L60 120\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"40\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Over: skyline head</text>\n  <rect x=\"280\" y=\"60\" width=\"26\" height=\"182\" fill=\"#6b4f35\"/>\n  <polygon points=\"250,120 293,30 336,120\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"318\" cy=\"170\" r=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"306\" y=\"182\" width=\"30\" height=\"58\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M340 90 l12 12 l24 -28\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f6e3b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/>\n  <text x=\"300\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"17\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f6e3b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Around the side</text>\n  <text x=\"100\" y=\"276\" font-size=\"15\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">stay off the skyline</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Keep a tree between you and the deer. Look around it (Tip).</li></ul>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Hearing range chart in kilohertz. People hear up to about 20. White tailed deer in one study heard about 0.25 to 30, best at 4 to 8. A second study found deer hear past 50. Deer hear higher pitch than we do: zippers, Velcro and metal clinks are the giveaway.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"26\" font-size=\"16\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Who hears what (kilohertz)</text>\n  <line x1=\"90\" y1=\"200\" x2=\"390\" y2=\"200\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/>\n  <g font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"90\" y=\"220\">0</text><text x=\"150\" y=\"220\">10</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"220\">20</text><text x=\"270\" y=\"220\">30</text><text x=\"330\" y=\"220\">40</text><text x=\"390\" y=\"220\">50</text></g>\n  <g stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"1\" opacity=\".3\"><line x1=\"150\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"150\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"210\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"210\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"270\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"270\" y2=\"200\"/><line x1=\"330\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"200\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"8\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">People</text>\n  <rect x=\"90\" y=\"56\" width=\"120\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8a9a6b\"/>\n  <text x=\"8\" y=\"118\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Deer</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">study 1</text>\n  <rect x=\"92\" y=\"104\" width=\"178\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/>\n  <rect x=\"114\" y=\"104\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"126\" y=\"98\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\" text-anchor=\"middle\">best 4 to 8</text>\n  <text x=\"8\" y=\"168\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">Deer</text><text x=\"8\" y=\"184\" font-size=\"14\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">study 2</text>\n  <rect x=\"92\" y=\"154\" width=\"298\" height=\"24\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\" opacity=\".6\"/>\n  <text x=\"380\" y=\"171\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"end\">past 50</text>\n  <rect x=\"12\" y=\"236\" width=\"376\" height=\"54\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"258\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Sharp high sounds give you away:</text>\n  <text x=\"200\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#ffd34d\" text-anchor=\"middle\">zippers, Velcro, nylon, metal on metal</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Deer hear higher pitch than people <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A steady crunch, crunch sounds like a person (Tip).</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: hearing studies and noise, in full</summary><ul><li>White tailed deer hear about 0.25 to 30 kilohertz in one study, best at 4 to 8 kilohertz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>People hear up to about 20 kilohertz. Deer hear higher pitch than we do <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">75%</span>.</li><li>A second study found deer can hear even higher, past 50 kilohertz <span class=\"cert c-lo\" title=\"Certainty\">65%</span>.</li><li>Sharp, high sounds are the giveaway: zippers, Velcro, nylon scrape, metal on metal (Tip).</li><li>A snapped stick can sound like a deer. A steady crunch, crunch rhythm sounds like a person (Tip).</li><li>Mule deer hearing studies: none found. Assumption: similar.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Four ways to quiet your kit in a 2 by 2 grid: wear wool or brushed fleece, not hard nylon. Tape metal parts that clink, like sling swivels and buckles. Swap Velcro for buttons or magnets. Jump up and down at the truck and fix anything that rattles.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <g fill=\"#dfe6d3\" stroke=\"#8a9a6b\" stroke-width=\"1.5\"><rect x=\"8\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"8\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\"/><rect x=\"8\" y=\"154\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\"/><rect x=\"204\" y=\"154\" width=\"188\" height=\"138\" rx=\"10\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M60 40 L140 40 L150 110 L50 110 Z\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><g stroke=\"#6b4f35\" stroke-width=\"2\"><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"55\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"55\"/><line x1=\"66\" y1=\"75\" x2=\"134\" y2=\"75\"/><line x1=\"62\" y1=\"95\" x2=\"138\" y2=\"95\"/></g>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Wool, not nylon</text>\n  <circle cx=\"270\" cy=\"70\" r=\"20\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"6\"/><rect x=\"286\" y=\"60\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"134\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Tape metal parts</text>\n  <rect x=\"50\" y=\"176\" width=\"44\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><path d=\"M60 196 l24 24 M84 196 l-24 24\" stroke=\"#c0392b\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"110\" y=\"176\" width=\"44\" height=\"60\" rx=\"4\" fill=\"#4a7fb0\"/><circle cx=\"132\" cy=\"206\" r=\"8\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <text x=\"102\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Velcro to buttons</text>\n  <circle cx=\"298\" cy=\"182\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/><rect x=\"288\" y=\"194\" width=\"20\" height=\"36\" rx=\"5\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <path d=\"M260 236 L336 236\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/><path d=\"M298 170 L298 160 M284 172 L278 164 M312 172 L318 164\" stroke=\"#e8590c\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <text x=\"298\" y=\"278\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Jump test at truck</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><ul><li>Jump up and down at the truck. Fix anything that rattles.</li></ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>More: clothing and kit, in full</summary><ul><li>Wool and brushed fleece are quieter in brush than hard nylon shells (Tip).</li><li>Tape or wrap metal parts that clink: sling swivels, buckles, knife sheath (Tip).</li><li>Swap Velcro pockets for buttons or magnets, or leave them open.</li><li>Before you leave the truck, jump up and down. Fix anything that rattles.</li><li>Keep the gun's action and safety quiet. Practise moving the safety slowly at home.</li></ul></details>","<figure class=\"diagram\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 400 300\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Mistake, top view. The hunter's eyes are fixed far ahead, a long narrow sight cone. A deer is bedded only 20 metres away, off to the side and outside the cone. Look near as well as far.\">\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#fffaf0\"/>\n  <rect width=\"400\" height=\"300\" fill=\"#dfe6d3\" opacity=\".5\"/>\n  <path d=\"M80 250 L330 30 L380 80 Z\" fill=\"#e8590c\" opacity=\".15\"/>\n  <circle cx=\"80\" cy=\"250\" r=\"10\" fill=\"#e8590c\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"284\" font-size=\"14\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\">You</text>\n  <g transform=\"translate(150 260)\"><ellipse rx=\"16\" ry=\"8\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><circle cx=\"-12\" cy=\"-6\" r=\"6\" fill=\"#8b5a2b\"/><path d=\"M-14 -11 l-4 -8 M-9 -11 l2 -8\" stroke=\"#8b5a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g>\n  <path d=\"M92 254 L132 260\" stroke=\"#2f3a2b\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-dasharray=\"3 4\"/>\n  <text x=\"180\" y=\"266\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#c0392b\">bedded, 20 m (22 yd)</text>\n  <text x=\"250\" y=\"140\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#e8590c\">eyes only far</text>\n  <rect x=\"12\" y=\"12\" width=\"230\" height=\"34\" rx=\"8\" fill=\"#2f3a2b\"/>\n  <text x=\"127\" y=\"35\" font-size=\"15\" font-weight=\"bold\" fill=\"#fff\" text-anchor=\"middle\">Look near, then far (65%)</text>\n</svg>\n</figure><aside class=\"callout rule\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Grandpa's rule (wisdom, not law)</div><p>Grandpa's rule (wisdom): If you think you are going slow enough, halve it.</p></aside><aside class=\"callout mistake\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Common mistakes</div><ul><li>Hiking pace, called still hunting.</li><li>Looking only far and walking past a bedded deer at 20 m (22 yd).</li><li>A swishing nylon jacket and a Velcro rip near a feeding deer.</li></ul></aside><aside class=\"callout field\"><div class=\"callout-t\">Do this in the field</div><p>Still hunt 200 m (219 yd) of timber. Aim for 30 minutes or more. Your brother walks behind and names every noise.</p></aside>","<ul><li><a href=\"https://wildlife.onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.2193/2006-326\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">D'Angelo and others, 2007, Hearing range of white tailed deer by auditory brainstem response, Journal of Wildlife Management</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview of abstract)</li><li><a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/42438287_The_behavioral_audiogram_of_whitetail_deer_Odocoileus_virginianus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Heffner and Heffner, behavioral audiogram of whitetail deer (ResearchGate)</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://fieldandstream.com/stories/hunting/still-hunting\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Field and Stream: Mastering still hunting</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://nadeerhunter.com/7-steps-for-still-hunting/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">North American Deer Hunter: 7 steps for still hunting</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li><a href=\"https://prohunt.com/articles/still-hunting-techniques-guide/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ProHunt: Still hunting techniques guide</a>, checked 2026-10-01 (search preview)</li><li>Note: pace and cover advice is hunter experience, labelled Tip. Hearing figures are from peer reviewed studies.</li></ul>"]